[size=4]NMS Shipwright[/size]

A Windows app for designing, finding and editing No Man's Sky starships and corvettes, plus a
general save editor. It reads the ship generator out of your own copy of the game, so a seed in
the app builds exactly the ship the game builds.

[line]

[size=3]Ships[/size]
[list]
[*]Design a ship part by part, with a 3D preview that builds up as you choose. Cockpit, wings,
chin, skirt, thrusters and the rest, named the way the community names them.
[*]Find a seed that builds your design. The search runs on all cores and tests around 70 million
seeds a second, with a live estimate of how long it will take.
[*]Find that ship in a real star system near you, if you would rather fly to it than edit it in.
[*]Put a design straight into your save, as a new ship or over one you already own.
[*]Recolour any ship with the game's real paint sets and a live preview.
[*]Save designs as files and share them.
[/list]

[size=3]Corvettes[/size]
[list]
[*]See the corvette in your save drawn from the modules bolted to it, each one listed by its
in-game name and the position it stands at.
[*]Build one in a window of its own: a palette of 172 modules, drag to place, coloured arrows to
slide along one axis, rings and sliders to turn about any axis, eighty steps of undo.
[*]Parts snap together the way the game snaps them, using the game's own sockets.
[*]Or turn snapping off and put a module anywhere, at any angle, bolted to nothing. The build
menu's restrictions are checked while you build and never re-checked when a save is loaded, which
is what people have been using clipping tricks to achieve.
[*]Mirror a module across the centreline and the pair moves, turns and goes together.
[/list]

[size=3]Save editing[/size]
[list]
[*]Inventories: add, remove and fill any item, technology or substance, repair and recharge,
unlock slots.
[*]Unlock recipes, blueprints, words, milestones, expedition and Twitch rewards.
[*]Multi-tools, freighters, frigates, companions.
[*]Export and import the save as JSON, plus a raw editor for anything not covered by a screen.
[/list]

[line]

[size=3]Before you use it[/size]
[list]
[*][b]Turn Steam Cloud off for No Man's Sky[/b] while you edit, or the cloud copy is put back over
your edit and nothing you did shows up. This is the single most common reason an edit "does not
work".
[*]Quit the game before writing. The app refuses to write while it is running, because the game
would overwrite the file on exit.
[*]Every write makes a timestamped backup next to your save first.
[/list]

[size=3]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit.
[*]No Man's Sky installed. Steam, GOG and the Microsoft Store are all found automatically; you can
also point the app at the folder yourself.
[*]Nothing else. No Python, no runtime to install -- it uses the Edge WebView2 that Windows
already ships.
[/list]

[size=3]What is not included[/size]

No game files are shipped with this app and none are redistributed. Ship part data, item tables,
3D models and language text are all read from your own installed copy of the game at runtime.

[line]

Open source, MIT licensed. Source, issues and the full changelog:
[url=https://github.com/S-T-0-7/NMS-Shipwright]github.com/S-T-0-7/NMS-Shipwright[/url]

Built with [url=https://pypi.org/project/hgpaktool/]hgpaktool[/url] to read the game's archives and
[url=https://www.unicorn-engine.org/]Unicorn[/url] to run the game's own generator code offline.
